        "description": "Direct-descent geometry — Luna 9 did not enter lunar orbit, descending straight to the surface."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 3.005,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "First soft landing on the Moon — Oceanus Procellarum",
        "description": "1966-02-03. Retrorocket fired at 75 km altitude; airbag-cushioned capsule bounced + rolled to rest at Oceanus Procellarum (7.13°N, 64.37°W). Transmitted the first panoramic images from the lunar surface — settling whether the lunar regolith could support a lander's weight (NASA had feared it might sink, a fear that delayed Apollo lander design)."
      }
